<p class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</p>
<h1>50cc Motorbike Hanoi: Solo Travelers Daily Rental Planning</h1>
<p>A single well-planned day on a rented 50cc can cover more of Hanoi than a week of taxis, and the whole day costs less than most travelers tip in a month. The verified rate for a 50cc scooter is 200,000 VND per day, the counter at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien opens at 09:00 and closes at 21:00 every day, and between those two clock positions sits a day you can shape entirely around yourself. This guide is the solo traveler’s version of that day: how to budget it, how to sequence it, what to ask at the counter, and how to end it with a bike returned calmly and a body that still wants dinner.</p>
<p>It belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/">50cc motorbike rental hub for Hanoi</a>, next to the guide to <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/solo-travelers-choosing-a-50cc/">choosing a 50cc as a solo traveler</a>. For the wider price picture across bike classes and rental periods, read the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost overview</a>, and for rental basics like deposits and documents, start from the <a href="/faq/">rental FAQ</a>. Daily planning is the part of a solo trip where independence pays hardest: no committees, no compromises, and the freedom to spend the day exactly as planned, or exactly not as planned.</p>
<nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents"><ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">What a one-day 50cc plan looks like</a></li>
